// Per-agent OpenClaw config for one jobhunter agent (design 10.3 step 9, install.sh step 8; CLI route design 6.1).
//
// `jh.py install render-agents-patch` renders this object once per entry of openclaw/agents.json and writes
// {"agents": {"entries": {"<agent id>": <this object>}}} to state/install/agents.patch.json. install.sh then
// runs `openclaw config patch --file <that> --dry-run --json`, the real patch, `openclaw config validate`, and
// `jh.py install verify-exec-policy --fix` (the effective merge must say allowlist or deny, and ask off).
//
// Scope rule: only agents.entries["jobhunter-*"]. Never bindings, channels, agents.defaults or
// browser.defaultProfile. The renderer refuses any other top-level key.
//
// Placeholders:
//   a string that is exactly "__MODEL__", "__SKILLS__", "__TOOLS_ALLOW__", "__TOOLS_DENY__",
//   "__MODELS_RUNTIME__", "__EXEC_POLICY__" or "__ELEVATED__" is replaced by the typed value rendered from
//   agents.json ("__MODELS_RUNTIME__" is dropped on the API key route); inside other strings __WS__ (the
//   agent's workspace), __WS_ROOT__, __REPO__, __PY__, __ROLE__ and __AGENT_ID__ are replaced as text.
//
// "__EXEC_POLICY__" is always explicit, so a global setting cannot leak in through a missing key, and it holds
// `mode` only: OpenClaw 2026.9.5 and later refuse "mode" together with "security" or "ask" in one exec object, and a
// per-agent mode replaces any security and ask the agent would inherit from the global tools.exec. Agents with
// exec_policy allowlist get {"mode": "allowlist", "host": "gateway", "strictInlineEval": true, "safeBins": [],
// "safeBinTrustedDirs": []} (mode allowlist is security allowlist with ask off): one allowlist entry (python, the
// agent's own jh.py argPattern from openclaw/exec-approvals.json5.tmpl), every miss refused at once, never a
// question to a person. jobhunter-qc (exec_policy deny) gets {"mode": "deny", "safeBins": [],
// "safeBinTrustedDirs": []} (security deny, ask off). The rendered patch also carries "security": null and
// "ask": null, which delete those keys of an older install in the same write. Only
// `./install.sh --cli-tools native --i-accept-reduced-protection` (mode N, reduced protection) renders mode full
// for the four tool agents. "__ELEVATED__" is always {"enabled": false}. The effective values are read back
// after the patch (`jh.py install verify-exec-policy`: security allowlist or deny, ask off).
{
  "workspace": "__WS__",
  "model": "__MODEL__",
  "models": "__MODELS_RUNTIME__",
  "skills": "__SKILLS__",
  "tools": {
    "allow": "__TOOLS_ALLOW__",
    "deny": "__TOOLS_DENY__",
    "fs": {"workspaceOnly": true},
    "exec": "__EXEC_POLICY__",
    "elevated": "__ELEVATED__"
  },
  // no memory search for pipeline agents [verify key: agents.entries.*.memory.search]
  "memory": {"search": {"enabled": false}}
}
